f ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f4700d4e9f4ae"} {"question" "q-80826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=4(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={b}_{1}-7{b}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}-7({c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}-7{c}_{1}+14{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-7{c}_{1}+\\frac{29}{2}{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ \\frac{29}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f4700d4e9f4ae"} {"question" "q-80826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "77545e91064cd3230944b1ee29142dd1d60c63b6886a0614b018e152107cd067"} {"question" "q-80826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Aca