c$'s. From the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=2{b}_{2}-(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{6}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5{b}_{1}+8{b}_{2} \\\\  & =5(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2})+8(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{6}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{2}+4{c}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{2} \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f4700d4e9f4ae"} {"question" "q-81229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "77545e91064cd3230944b1ee29142dd1d60c63b6886a0614b018e152107cd067"} {"question" "q-81229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f4700d4e9f4ae"} {"question" "q-81229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course