{R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=-4{b}_{1}+5{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f4700d4e9f4ae"} {"question" "q-112833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=-4{b}_{1}+5{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Multiplying the second equation by $5$ and adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+5{c}_{2}=6{b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{6}{c}_{1}+\\frac{5}{6}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=-4(\\frac{1}{6}{c}_{1}+\\frac{5}{6}{c}_{2})+5{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{2}{6}{c}_{1}+\\frac{4}{6}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3{b}_{1}-6{b}_{2} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{6}{c}_{1}+\\frac{5}{6}{c}_{2})-6(\\frac{2}{6}{c}_{1}+\\frac{4}{6}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{5}{2}{c}_{2}-2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{3}{2}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f4700d4e9f4ae"} {"question" "q-112833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256