ear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f4700d4e9f4ae"} {"question" "q-80838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}-{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=3{b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=2(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2})+{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}-\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6{b}_{1}-{b}_{2} \\\\  & =6(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2})-(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}-\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{8}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f4700d4e9f4ae"} {"question" "q-80838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "77545e91064cd3230944b1ee29142dd1d60c63b6886a0614b018e152107cd067"} {"question" "q-80838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065354/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdcf62b9e4cf2de243eec3278bab94630d43a04c7495c894851f